# LRU Cache in Rust

An LRU (Least Recently Used) cache needs O(1) lookups *and* O(1) updates. The classic approach combines a **HashMap** (for O(1) key→value lookup) with a **doubly-linked list** (for O(1) reordering).

Let me build this up, and I'll highlight the ownership pitfalls along the way.

## The Core Design

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::collections::hash_map::Entry;
use std::hash::Hash;
use std::marker::PhantomData;

struct Node<K, V> {
    key: K,
    value: V,
    prev: Option<NodeRef<K, V>>,
    next: Option<NodeRef<K, V>>,
}

type NodeRef<K, V> = &'mut Node<K, V>;
```

